From: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: reinit gamepad MCU on resume from suspend

The RSInput serdev gamepad MCU loses its state across system suspend (deep
S2RAM): after resume the controller produces no input until the init command
sequence is re-sent. Add a .resume PM callback that re-runs
rsinput_init_commands() so the gamepad works again after resume.

Ported from tiopex's SM8750 ROCKNIX fix (0508-input-rsinput-add-pm-resume-to-
reinit-mcu-after-suspend) to the SM8550 / AYN Thor build.
diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
index 20ae067..4772c23 100644
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -612,6 +612,15 @@ static void rsinput_remove(struct serdev_device *serdev) {
     regulator_disable(drv->vdd);
 }
 
+static int rsinput_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+    struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+    return rsinput_init_commands(drv);
+}
+
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rsinput_pm_ops, NULL, rsinput_resume);
+
 static const struct of_device_id rsinput_of_match[] = {
     { .compatible = "gamepad,rsinput" },
     { /* sentinel */ }
@@ -624,6 +633,7 @@ static struct serdev_device_driver rsinput_driver = {
     .driver = {
         .name = "rsinput",
         .of_match_table = rsinput_of_match,
+        .pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&rsinput_pm_ops),
     },
 };
 
